1438+  89E5                     .sbttl "Trip Plate Action Routine"
1439+  89E5             ;****************************************************
1440+  89E5             ;* This routine is called from 'colobj' in TWMot    
1441+  89E5             ;* and is used to set off the fire balls when a     
1442+  89E5             ;* trip plate is stepped on.                        
1443+  89E5             ;* Each maze may have up to 8 trip plates. The      
1444+  89E5             ;* plate index, through the maze number, through    
1445+  89E5             ;* the 'difcty' level will obtain the trip plate    
1446+  89E5             ;* table entry.                                     
1447+  89E5             ;* Each Entry Contains the Following:              
1448+  89E5             ;*  XH,YH,XV,YV                                   
1449+  89E5             ;* One or Two fireballs will be started (if available)     
1450+  89E5             ;* at the X,Y location specified. They will be      
1451+  89E5             ;* offset from each other depending on their        
1452+  89E5             ;* velocities.                                      
1453+  89E5             ;*                                                  
1454+  89E5             ;* Inputs: X=ztrpp+index (to current plate hit)     
1455+  89E5             ;*                                                  
1456+  89E5             ;* Note: This routine must not use temp9!!!         
1457+  89E5             ;****************************************************
1458+  89E5 20 A0 8A    trpoint jsr chkall      ;Make sure this guy didn't fire any
